{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"467d5baa597396f6","name":"card_event_dark_deeds","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Finland/events/card_event_dark_deeds","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"DARK DEEDS","text":"Add a SISSI to your support line. Draw a card. Discard it at the end of your next turn.","flavorText":"As the Soviets were planning to invade Finland in late 1939, the Finnish military prepared for a harsh winter, which ultimately became the coldest in over a century. The Finns spent most of the autumn destroying infrastructure like bridges, roads, houses and barns that had taken decades to build. Their goal was to deny the Soviets any shelter or resources during their advance. This scorched earth strategy left abandoned villages and towns in ruins, making them inhospitable even to the enemy. Finns set booby traps everywhere: mines were hidden in haystacks, under outhouse seats, in abandoned sleds, and even inside dead animals. They poisoned wells or, when time and resources were limited, contaminated them with horse manure. Floating mines were placed under newly-frozen lakes to detonate under Soviet troops as they advanced across the ice.","faction":"Finland","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_dark_deeds","title":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_dark_deeds_title","SourceString":"DARK DEEDS","LocalizedString":"DARK DEEDS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Finland","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_dark_deeds_text","SourceString":"Add a SISSI to your support line. Draw a card. Discard it at the end of your next turn.","LocalizedString":"Add a SISSI to your support line. Draw a card. Discard it at the end of your next turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_dark_deeds_history","SourceString":"As the Soviets were planning to invade Finland in late 